Flutter Team Handoff — Priority Recommendations (Frontend to match Backend)

Goal
- Ensure the app consistently communicates dual-role P2P behavior: every student can browse, post, and message in the same session.
- Align frontend copy, IA, and API usage with the live backend.

Priority 1 — Critical copy fixes (role neutrality)
1) Replace all “vendor” wording in chat UI
   - Current risky text: “Start a conversation with vendor”.
   - Replace with: “Start a conversation with {fullName}” or “Message {fullName}”.
   - Source of truth for names:
     - Conversation list: counterpartFullName
     - Browse/search cards: ownerFullName
     - Public profile endpoint: fullName

2) Update onboarding/login copy to reflect dual role
   - Avoid buyer-only framing like “find a good deal” as the sole message.
   - Suggested helper line: “Browse listings or post your own item anytime.”
   - Step label “Browse” (step 3) can become neutral: “Start” or “Trade”.

Priority 2 — Data-contract alignment (must implement)
3) Render poster identity on listing cards
   - Backend now returns ownerFullName in listing card payloads.
   - Apply to Browse, Search Results, Nearby, Zone and Feed cards.
   - Endpoint family:
     - GET /api/v1/listings/search
     - GET /api/v1/listings/nearby
     - GET /api/v1/listings/zone/{tag}
     - GET /api/v1/listings/feed

4) Use public profile endpoint for trust cards
   - Endpoint: GET /api/v1/users/{id}/public
   - Returns: id, fullName, campus, activeListingsCount, memberSince
   - Use this for profile preview sheets/pages before initiating chat.

5) Keep conversation creation contract updated
   - POST /api/v1/conversations returns role-neutral fields:
     - id, listingId, listingTitle, inquirerUserId, posterUserId, createdAt, updatedAt
   - Do not expect old buyerUserId/sellerUserId fields.

Priority 3 — UX consistency with backend states
6) Respect listing availability in messaging CTAs
   - Backend blocks messaging for SOLD and DELETED listings.
   - Error codes:
     - LISTING_SOLD
     - LISTING_UNAVAILABLE
   - Frontend behavior:
     - Disable “Chat Now/Message” for unavailable items.
     - Show status badge and clear reason text.

7) Saved Items / Bookmarks state handling
   - Bookmark payload includes status string; use it to gate CTA.
   - If status is SOLD/DELETED:
     - Disable chat CTA
     - Keep Remove enabled

Priority 4 — Navigation/IA reinforcement
8) Keep buy/sell always one tap apart
   - Maintain persistent bottom nav (Browse/Search/Sell/Chat/Account).
   - Add “My Conversations” visibility in Account area (if missing) to balance “My Listings”.

9) Remove placeholder text in production empty states
   - Replace “Maps API Integration Point” with production-safe empty state copy:
     - “No items found in this category yet.”
     - Optional secondary action: “Switch to List View”.

