Screen-to-Endpoint Contract Map

A) Browse Home + Search Results + Category List View
- Endpoint(s):
   - GET /api/v1/listings/feed
   - GET /api/v1/listings/search
   - GET /api/v1/listings/nearby
   - GET /api/v1/listings/zone/{tag}
- Must render from payload:
   - title, priceUgx, locationText/campus, primaryImageUrl, ownerFullName

B) Listing Card “Message/Chat Now” action
- Flow:
   1. POST /api/v1/conversations { listingId }
   2. Navigate to chat screen using returned conversation id
- Handle conflict errors:
   - LISTING_SOLD
   - LISTING_UNAVAILABLE

C) Chat List Screen
- Endpoint:
   - GET /api/v1/conversations?page=&size=
- Use:
   - counterpartFullName, lastMessageBody, lastMessageAt, counterpartActiveNow

D) Chat Thread Screen
- Endpoints:
   - GET /api/v1/conversations/{conversationId}/messages?limit=
   - GET /api/v1/conversations/{conversationId}/messages/long-poll?afterMessageId=&timeoutSeconds=
   - POST /api/v1/conversations/{conversationId}/messages

E) Poster Preview / Trust Sheet
- Endpoint:
   - GET /api/v1/users/{id}/public
- Show:
   - fullName, campus, activeListingsCount, memberSince

F) My Listings Screen
- Endpoint:
   - GET /api/v1/listings/my?status=ALL|ACTIVE|SOLD|DELETED
- Use status + actions to drive buttons:
   - ACTIVE  => Edit/Delete/Sell
   - SOLD    => Read-only sold state
   - DELETED => Restore/Purge

Quick Parsing Snippets (pseudo)

ListingCardModel.fromJson
- ownerFullName: json['ownerFullName'] as String?

ConversationCreateResponse.fromJson
- inquirerUserId: json['inquirerUserId'] as int
- posterUserId: json['posterUserId'] as int

PublicUserProfile.fromJson
- id: json['id'] as int
- fullName: json['fullName'] as String
- campus: json['campus'] as String?
- activeListingsCount: json['activeListingsCount'] as int
- memberSince: DateTime.parse(json['memberSince'] as String)

